    {
      "filename": "Ajax Peak, San Juan Mountains, Telluride, Colorado 2014.jpg",
      "title": "File:Ajax Peak, San Juan Mountains, Telluride, Colorado 2014.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c9/Ajax_Peak%2C_San_Juan_Mountains%2C_Telluride%2C_Colorado_2014.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajax_Peak,_San_Juan_Mountains,_Telluride,_Colorado_2014.jpg",
      "width": 11400,
      "height": 11525,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Zach Dischner",
      "description": "This was taken up by Telluride's Bridal Veil falls, looking back down the valley. For those who haven't been to Telluride, the place is fu&amp;*&amp;@#$ amazing. Little town in a HUGE landscape. All I could think when I got to this spot was \"Holy shit, this is just MASSIVE!\" (I can't censor direct quotes, its unethical). Looking back down the valley, its almost impossible to take in. \nIf you look in the bottom right 1/3 of the shot, you can see my truck, parked along the windy road. There's also a banana for scale, but its so small you can't see it. \nTo make sure I got the scale right, I made this shot out of about 50 shots, taken in a a raster scan of the mountain, at around 70mm. Its just so big a single shot couldn't do it justice.  \nZach Rides a Bike\n\nCheck out the 2manventure stoke report",
      "dateCreated": "2014-08-02 17:56",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "telluride-colorado-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9wg8"
    },
